 \\, \\text{miles}\\)):  \n- **Walking time**: \\(\\frac{1.5 \\, \\text{miles}}{3 \\, \\text{mph}} = 0.5 \\, \\text{hours} = 30 \\, \\text{minutes}\\).  \n- **Running time**: \\(\\frac{1.5 \\, \\text{miles}}{6 \\, \\text{mph}} = 0.25 \\, \\text{hours} = 15 \\, \\text{minutes}\\).  \n- **Total time**: \\(30 + 15 = 45 \\, \\text{minutes}\\).\n\n**Answer**: \\(\\boxed{D}\\) (45 minutes).", "ground_truth_solution": ": \n\n1. **Determine the distances and times for Angus:**\n\n    - Angus walks for half the time and runs for the other half. Total time taken by Angus is 40 minutes.\n    - Since he walks for half the time:\n      \\[\n      \\text{Walking time} = \\frac{40}{2} = 20 \\text{ minutes}\n      \\]\n      \\[\n      \\text{Running time} = \\frac{40}{2} = 20 \\text{ minutes}\n      \\]\n\n    - Convert time into hours since speeds are given in miles per hour (mph):\n      \\[\n      20 \\text{ minutes} = \\frac{20}{60} \\text{ hours} = \\frac{1}{3} \\text{ hours}\n      \\]\n    - Calculate the distance walked by Angus:\n      \\[\n      \\text{Distance walked} = 3 \\text{ mph} \\times \\frac{1}{3} \\text{ hours} = 1 \\text{ mile}\n      \\]\n    - Calculate the distance run by Angus:\n      \\[\n      \\text{Distance run} = 6 \\text{ mph} \\times \\frac{1}{3} \\text{ hours} = 2 \\text{ miles}\n      \\]\n    - Total distance covered by Angus:\n      \\[\n      \\text{Total distance} = 1 \\text{ mile} + 2 \\text{ miles} = 3 \\text{ miles}\n      \\]\n\n2. **Determine the distances and times for Bruce:**\n\n    - Bruce covers half the distance by walking and the other half by running. The total distance is the same as Angus\u2019s total distance which is 3 miles.\n    - Calculate the distance walked by Bruce:\n      \\[\n      \\text{Distance walked} = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5 \\text{ miles}\n      \\]\n    - Calculate the time taken to walk:\n      \\[\n      \\text{Time to walk} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} = \\frac{1.5 \\text{ miles}}{3 \\text{ mph}} = 0